Cargohold now needs access to PostgreSQL (Backup API). Its helm values require `postgresql`, `postgresqlPool` and optionally `postgresqlPassword` (secret `pgPassword`), as well as a `galley` endpoint (set by the chart). The tables are created by brig's `migrate-postgres` (cargohold does not run migrations). Make sure the S3 prefix `backups/` has no lifecycle rules.
The S3 credentials of cargohold additionally need `s3:ListBucketMultipartUploads` and `s3:AbortMultipartUpload` on the bucket: failed backup uploads abort their unfinished multipart uploads (without these permissions the parts leak; an error is logged).
Backup deletion removes all object versions and delete markers on versioned S3 buckets. The S3 credentials of cargohold additionally need `s3:GetBucketVersioning`, `s3:ListBucketVersions`, `s3:ListBucket` and `s3:DeleteObjectVersion`.
